        "original_id": "1766dc40-3a70-5a42-9c25-1a4b924a8beb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Emperor Shōwa, Hirohito\n- Events: Greenery Day\n- Places: Japan\n- Concepts: Hirohito's name meaning\n\nFacts:\n- During the Shōwa era, Japan celebrated Emperor Shōwa's birthday on April 29 every year.\n- The present observation of Greenery Day in Japan as a national holiday stems from the celebration of Emperor Shōwa's birthday on April 29 during the Shōwa era.\n- Hirohito is the personal name of Emperor Shōwa.\n- The name Hirohito means \"abundant benevolence\".",
